  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 25.567,
   "duration": 15.523,
   "text": "Why does this always work? Each L has one new row, one new column, and one corner. For the fifth square, that is four, plus four, plus one: nine. In general, the n-th L has two n minus one squares. That is exactly the n-th odd number.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "parts": 27.344,
    "law": 34.73
   },
   "scene": "OddSquares"
  },
  {
